Package: RoDPAA
Title: Robust Dissimilarity-Based Principal Angle Analysis for Multiview
    Data
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Yanyan", "Xu", , "xyylilian@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Yue", "Wang", role = "aut")
  )
Description: Unsupervised integration of two high-dimensional data views
    measured on the same participants. Each view is represented by a
    user-chosen dissimilarity (for example Bray-Curtis or Euclidean),
    converted to a centred similarity matrix, and summarised by its
    leading eigenvectors. Principal angles between the two signal
    subspaces quantify cross-view alignment, a permutation test that
    breaks participant correspondence estimates how many directions are
    shared, and the significant direction pairs are averaged into
    participant-level shared factors. The framework is designed to
    identify both completely and partially aligned shared structure.
